WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:04.541
C# 14 shipped with .NET 10, the long-term support release.

00:04.591 --> 00:10.452
Here are its best features, in VS Code with SharpLsp: free C# and F# tooling.

00:10.502 --> 00:13.785
Install SharpLsp from the VS Code Marketplace.

00:13.835 --> 00:16.601
Subscribe for .NET, C# and F# content.

00:17.051 --> 00:21.036
Feature one: extension members. Open an extension block for any type...

00:21.086 --> 00:27.049
...and put properties in it, not just methods. Hover it, and SharpLsp shows exactly what you declared.

00:30.851 --> 00:32.980
Now every string has an IsBlank property.

00:33.030 --> 00:37.793
Completion offers it right beside the built-in members, and it reads like it was always there.

00:37.843 --> 00:41.728
And hover tells you exactly where it lives: the extension block on string.

00:44.384 --> 00:47.320
Hit F12, and you land straight on the extension block.

00:52.651 --> 00:57.138
Feature two: the field keyword. Give a setter a body, with no backing field to declare.

00:57.188 --> 01:01.660
The word field means the one the compiler makes for you. Every name now gets trimmed.

01:04.117 --> 01:09.985
Feature three: null-conditional assignment. Question-mark-dot works on the left of an equals sign, too.

01:10.035 --> 01:14.178
If Address is null, the assignment just doesn't happen. No if statement needed.

01:15.251 --> 01:21.533
Extension members, the field keyword, and null-conditional assignment. That's C# 14 on .NET 10.

01:21.983 --> 01:26.609
Install SharpLsp, and subscribe for .NET, C# and F# content!
